BanMido wrote:
>
> In my current neutral ranger game, so far, I have found *four* temples to 
> Mars, i.e. chaotic (not including the one in Minetown, which incidentally, 
> is chaotic too). The four temples are located on dungeon levels 10, 15, 23 
> and 25. This is in addition to a chaotic altar generated on level 5, which I 
> did convert.

I value altars enough that if I do not find one by some point I'll go
back and convert the mine town one.  What that point is varies for me
year to year.  I've killed the mine town priest on the way back up from
mines end in some games.  I've gotten to Medusa and gone back in the
occasional game with no other altar until then.

> Perhaps, it is daring me to convert the altar at a cross-aligned temple, a 
> task I have never attempted before.

As long as you have one co-aligned (converted) altar you don't have a
strict need to do that.  Maybe you want to do it for fun, though.  As
long as you have a way to recover the luck, the alignment points and the
telepathy it's not that difficult.  There are a few ways that get
discussed every so often.  One is the boulder manuever method.  One is
the thrown missile method that takes carving out one of the walls and a
ton of missiles.  One is the brute force go in and duke it out and
suffer the damage method.  If you let your pet do the killing even
better.


